% SOURCE: ICOT TR-524, K. Yoshida, "The SIMPOS Distributed File System -- Its Design and Implementation", Nov. 1989
% PDF page 12, printed folio 11. Section 3.4.1 "Interface Primitives Based on Asynchronous-Communication", two in-text
% examples (no figure numbers). The second continues on PDF p13 (tr0524_p13.esp).
% Transcribed by eye from 300dpi crops (A/work/tr0524/x12a.png, x12b.png). The quote marks are printed as TeX
% double quotes `` and '' ; reproduced here as two backquote/apostrophe characters.

% (1) "a program to make a new file, named ``>sys>user>gee>humm.txt'', and append a string ``To be, '' to the file:"
:make(#binary_file, File, ``>sys>user>gee>humm.txt''),
:add_data(File, ``To be, ''),
:close(File),

% (2) "preparing external accessors for overlapping operations as follows:"
:open(#binary_file, File, ``>sys>user>gee>humm.txt'', shared, immediate),
:accessor(File, Acc),               % attach an external accessor
:put_data(File, ``or ''),           % put ``or '' in internal accessor
:submit_add(File, ID1, suppress),
